From fc55ce46162a347f92ccae95684cf69aeb338b6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:07:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: clemente: populate the FRU EEPROMs

Back 24 of the 27 FRU EEPROMs with images read from hardware, so guest
firmware can identify the HPMs, the CPU and boot drives, the SCM, BSM,
PDB, HMC, both OCP NICs, both IO mezzanines and both E1.S backplanes
instead of finding them blank. The two module aux EEPROMs were erased
on the sampled chassis and the second mezzanine's OSFP FRU was absent,
so those three stay blank.

The E1.S backplane and IO mezzanine helpers each serve two instances
carrying different images, so both now take a descriptor naming the
EEPROMs they install.

The content is sanitized: part and serial numbers masked, dates fixed,
asset tags replaced, distinct originals kept distinct. Several images
carry OEM MultiRecords whose contents are undocumented; the records are
kept and their bodies zeroed.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
---
 hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_clemente.c | 974 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 948 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_clemente.c b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_clemente.c
index f983b9e021..21646af6bd 100644
